.TITLE "taskkill"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Ends one or more tasks or processes. Processes can be ended by process ID or image name, making it a powerful tool for __process management__.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**taskkill /pid 1234**
Ends the process with the specified process ID.
> __/pid 1234__ the target PID

**taskkill /im notepad.exe**
Ends the process with the specified image name.
> __/im notepad.exe__ the target image name

**taskkill /f /im notepad.exe**
Forcefully ends the specified process.
> __/f__ force flag

**taskkill /t /im notepad.exe**
Ends the specified process and any child processes started by it.
> __/t__ tree kill flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Use the __/f__ flag only when a process is unresponsive and cannot be closed normally. Forcefully ending processes may lead to __unsaved data loss__.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**windows:tasklist** **windows:systeminfo**

documentation: __https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/taskkill__
